Patches to the grimoire, applied in the build chroot by "cauldron toolchain"
(cauldron_sorcerous_cauldron_defaults) after the grimoires are downloaded:
patch -p0 relative to the build chroot's root, so paths look like
var/lib/sorcery/codex/test/<section>/<spell>/<file>. One directory per spell,
files named <spell>.patch. Keep them few and temporary: each should be
reported to the grimoire maintainers and dropped once the grimoire is fixed.

  parted          gcc 16 rejects incompatible pointer types (parted 3.6)
  squashfs-tools  same (squashfs-tools 4.4); needed to package the ISO
  grub2           grub-default sets GRUB_DISABLE_UUID, which GRUB doesn't
                  know (it's GRUB_DISABLE_LINUX_UUID); grub-mkconfig then
                  writes root=UUID=, which needs an initramfs SMGL doesn't
                  make, so the installed system can't find its root. Use
                  root=PARTUUID= (the kernel handles it by itself) instead.
                  Also GRUB_BACKGROUND="smgl-splash.png": grub-mkconfig
                  tests the path as given (relative to wherever it runs),
                  so the splash the spell installs to /boot/grub never
                  shows; use the full path. And the splash is a 4-bit palette
                  PNG, which GRUB 2.12 silently doesn't draw:
                  files/.../smgl-splash.png is the same image as 8-bit RGB
                  (a hack's files/ directory mirrors the build chroot's root
                  and is copied over it before the patches are applied)
  wireless-regdb  installs only the CRDA file (regulatory.bin); kernels since
                  4.15 read /lib/firmware/regulatory.db + .p7s (without them
                  wifi falls back to the restrictive world regulatory domain)
  wpa_supplicant  2.11 doesn't build against OpenSSL 4 (ASN1_STRING became
                  opaque); adds a patch using ASN1_STRING_get0_data/_length
                  in src/crypto/tls_openssl.c (distributions carry the same
                  fix, e.g. LFS' wpa_supplicant-2.11-openssl_4_fixes-1.patch)
  dosfstools      4.2 only installs mkfs.fat/fsck.fat; adds a BUILD with
                  --enable-compat-symlinks, so mkfs.vfat and fsck.vfat exist
                  (fsck at boot looks for fsck.vfat for a vfat fstab entry;
                  documentation and the installer say mkfs.vfat)
  openssh         "make install" runs ssh-keygen -A on the build machine (the
                  keys end up in the spell's cache, shared by every system
                  installed from it) and only installs ssh_config/sshd_config
                  if they don't exist yet (so caches built on a system that
                  has them lack them). Use install-nosysconf +
                  install_config_file, and let the init script make the
                  host keys on first start (like the systemd unit does)
                  Also: run "systemctl daemon-reload" only when systemd is
                  running (it fails in a chroot after systemd is cast)

The next three are for the systemd install (installer, network variant).
cauldron's simpleinit build never casts them, but the build chroot's
grimoire, hacks included, is what system.tar.xz carries:
  systemd         254.27: "depends dbus" -> "runtime_depends -sub SYSTEMD
                  dbus" (systemd has its own sd-bus; libdbus is only for its
                  tests), so dbus is cast after systemd and with systemd
                  support; policykit becomes a suggest_depends (polkit is
                  only used at run time and itself needs libsystemd);
                  cryptsetup -> cryptsetup-luks (the 2004 spell); gnu-efi
                  (unused since v253) -> pyelftools for bootloader=true
                  (systemd-boot, systemd-stub, bootctl), which BUILD pairs
                  with efi=true; man pages via optional docbook-xsl instead
                  of man=auto (which failed without the stylesheets); ACL
                  only from the acl dependency (CONFIGURE set it a second
                  time)
  dbus            SUB_DEPENDS/PRE_SUB_DEPENDS for SYSTEMD (forces its
                  optional systemd dependency on; used by systemd above)
  policykit       128 doesn't use dbus-glib or python3 (dropped); dbus is a
                  run-time dependency; perl and gettext are used but weren't
                  declared; no 0.9x "polkituser" account
  jinja2          3.1.6 builds with the flit_core backend but doesn't depend
                  on flit-core (needed by systemd)
  linux-pam       1.7.3 passes docs=enabled when PAM_DOCS=y but nothing
                  otherwise, so meson's "auto" builds the docs whenever
                  xmllint/xsltproc are installed (libxslt is in the base
                  system); their validation fetches http://docbook.org/... and
                  fails offline. Pass docs=disabled
